[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should the design set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests (node:test)
  [38;5;246mBuilt-in runner, zero dependencies, plus a `npm test` script. Needed for the session module tests described above. [39m
  [38;5;246mRecommended.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Lint + format (Biome)
  [38;5;246mOne dev dependency covering both, with `npm run lint` / `npm run format`. Recommended; cheapest to adopt before the [39m
  [38;5;246mcodebase grows.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests (Playwright)
  [38;5;246mWould cover the DOM wiring that unit tests skip. Adds a browser download and real CI weight for a six-file project.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Fuzz / mutation testing
  [38;5;246mLittle to chew on in a project this size; I would defer this.[39m
